 ## `parallel/log.decomposePar`
 Real `decomposePar -force` log (ESI OpenFOAM v2606) of the shared coarse sphere mesh (192220 cells) with the app's solver files and `system/decomposeParDict` (numberOfSubdomains 4, method scotch), written while checking the clean stop in parallel (D-063): cells per processor 47575, 47582, 48530 and 48533, 6396 processor faces in total, "Max number of cells = 48533 (0.994694% above average 48055)". Only the Host, PID and Case lines were sanitized.
 
+
+## `freestream_run/` (`massFlow_<patch>.dat`, `summary.json`)
+Real output (ESI OpenFOAM v2606) of tests/test_far_field.py::test_slip_against_freestream_far_field_at_ten_degrees (marker `long`, D-065): the flattened ellipsoid `pv.ParametricEllipsoid(0.5, 0.5, 0.15, u_res=48, v_res=24, w_res=24).triangulate().clean()` (part `Body`) meshed with the default `Domain()` and `Mesh()` (192458 cells), `simpleFoam` with the app's solver files at 20 m/s and alpha 10 deg on 4 cores, criteria Cd and Cl asymptotic (window 50, tolerance 0.01), limit 600 iterations, with the freestream far field. `massFlow_<patch>.dat` are the unchanged `postProcessing/massFlow_<patch>/0/surfaceFieldValue.dat` files of that run (inlet, outlet, sides, top, bottom; sum(phi) per iteration, no paths in their headers). `summary.json` is written by the same test: Cl, Cd (last iteration and the mean / range over the last 50), mass balance, iterations and end state of the slip and the freestream runs.
